$WW,1$$FG,4$$TX+CX,"Infernal Demands"$$FG$

AntichristOS is a toy, and toys do not get to make demands.  But if the computer industry is ever taking requests from the basement, here is the list, written on the back of a concert ticket.

* Keep PS/2 keyboard and mouse emulation switched on in the BIOS.  A 64-bit hobby operating system with one $LK,"keyboard",A="FI:::/Kernel/SerialDev/Keyboard.HC"$ driver and one $LK,"mouse",A="FI:::/Kernel/SerialDev/Mouse.HC"$ driver should still be able to hear you scream.

* Virtual machines: keep the hard drive at the IDE primary master, $FG,2$1F0/3F6$FG$, and the CD/DVD at the secondary master, $FG,2$170/376$FG$.  Then $LK,"::/Kernel/BlkDev/DskATAId.HC"$ can stop wandering the halls looking for them.

* Keep legacy BIOS boot alive in virtual machines.  AntichristOS boots from the same $LK,"CD-DVD-Boot-Loader",A="FI:::/Adam/Opt/Boot/BootDVD.HC"$ it always did.

* Every PC speaker, everywhere, must remain able to play a tritone.  Hymns too.

* Every record player must keep a switch that turns the platter backwards.  Some of us have research to do.

* Should there ever be a factory ROM with AntichristOS in it, there will be just an English version -- and a backmasked one, which is the same version, read in a mirror.  Other countries can make their own.

* Datasheets in $LK,"DolDoc",A="FI:::/Doc/DolDocOverview.DD"$ format, please, with links that work.  $LK,"LinkChk",A="MN:LinkChk"$() is watching.

* Somebody should still write a proper $LK,"Spell Checker",A="FI:::/Demo/SuggestSpelling.HC"$.  Blasphemy is easier to forgive when it is spelled correctly.

* We will make a $LK,"Standard AntichristOS PC",A="FI:::/Doc/StdAntichristOSPC.DD"$.  It will be black.
